# OPT-IN: blanket NOPASSWD sudo for andrew. NOT installed by bootstrap.sh.
#
# Trade-off: with this file installed, anyone who SSHes as andrew gets
# silent root with no further authentication. The default jinx posture
# (sudoers/00-andrew = ALL=(ALL) ALL, scoped NOPASSWD per project via
# sudoers/<project> — see sudoers/nabu for the canonical pattern) keeps
# password-required sudo for ad-hoc commands and grants NOPASSWD only
# for the specific systemctl invocations that deploy scripts need to run
# unattended.
#
# Use this file when you're iterating quickly on box configuration
# during a project bootstrap and the password prompts get in the way.
# Remove it when you're done. RUNBOOK.md § "Developer convenience:
# blanket NOPASSWD" has the operational details.
#
# Lexical-order note: /etc/sudoers.d/ files are processed in sorted
# order. The 01- prefix puts this file after 00-andrew, so the
# NOPASSWD: ALL grant takes precedence over the password-required
# directive in 00-andrew. Snapshot-restore re-applying both files is
# safe — sudoers semantics are deterministic on order.
#
# Install:  sudo install -m 0440 -o root -g root \
#             01-andrew-nopasswd /etc/sudoers.d/01-andrew-nopasswd
# Validate: sudo visudo -cf /etc/sudoers.d/01-andrew-nopasswd
# Remove:   sudo rm /etc/sudoers.d/01-andrew-nopasswd
#
# CI's visudo-check job (.github/workflows/lint.yml) validates this
# file's syntax independently of whether it is ever installed.
andrew ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
